I am in a big clothes shop in the city.
There is a lot of crowd in the shop.
The real monsoon will start soon.
I want a good raincoat for the Mumbai rains.
I go to the shopkeeper.
"Dada, show me a good raincoat," I say.
He shows me a blue raincoat.
I look at that raincoat.
But that raincoat is a little small.
"Do you have a bigger raincoat than this?" I ask.
"Yes madam, look at this black raincoat," Dada says.
This black raincoat is big.
It is also thicker than the blue raincoat.
The Mumbai rains are very heavy.
Therefore I need a sturdy raincoat.
"Is this black raincoat sturdy?" I ask.
"Yes madam, this lasts very well in the rain," he tells me.
I like this big raincoat.
"Give me this very raincoat," I say.
I pay the money and buy that raincoat.
